relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000193 ! endomesoderm
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000053 ! vegetal hemisphere

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000489
name: embryonic endoderm
def: "The endoderm that is specifically present in an embryo." []
is_a: ECAO:2000485 ! endoderm
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000484 ! presumptive endoderm
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000008 ! embryo

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000490
name: larval endoderm
def: "The endoderm that is specifically present in a larva." []
is_a: ECAO:2000485 ! endoderm
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000489 ! embryonic endoderm
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000012 ! larva

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000491
name: pre-metamorphic organism endoderm
def: "The endoderm that is specifically present in an embryo post-gastrulation and a larva but not in an adult." []
is_a: ECAO:2000485 ! endoderm
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000013 ! pre-metamorphic organism

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000492
name: vegetal plate
def: "A thickened region (or placode) at the vegetal pole of the blastula that contains prospective mesoderm and endoderm. The cells of the vegetal plate will be internalized during gastrulation." []
synonym: "VgP" RELATED []
is_a: ECAO:2000018 ! embryonic region
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000053 ! vegetal hemisphere

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000493
name: bottle cell
def: "A characteristic early embryonic cell with a bottle or flask shape.  In some echinoderms, bottle cells are found in the vegetal plate and initiate its invagination at the time of archenteron development." []
xref: CL:0007020
is_a: ECAO:2000135 ! embryonic cell
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000492 ! vegetal plate

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000494
name: archenteron
def: "The invaginated tube of a gastrula embryo that will give rise to the larval digestive tract." []
synonym: "primordial digestive tube" RELATED []
synonym: "primitive digestive tract" RELATED []
synonym: "primitive gut" RELATED []
synonym: "embryonic gut" RELATED []
xref: UBERON:0004735
is_a: ECAO:2000001 ! anatomical structure
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000492 ! vegetal plate
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000008 ! embryo

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000495
name: archenteron tip
def: "The anterior territory of the archenteron." []
synonym: "archenteron roof" RELATED []
synonym: "anterior archenteron" RELATED []
synonym: "tip of archetron" RELATED []
xref: UBERON:3010432
is_a: ECAO:2000018 ! embryonic region
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000494 ! archenteron

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000496
name: archenteron wall
def: "The layer of cells that form the archenteron, but at the level of its anterior tip and that of the blastopore." []
is_a: ECAO:2000026 ! embryonic structure
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000494 ! archenteron

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000497
name: blastopore
def: "The orifice of invagination of the endomesodermal cells during the embryonic stages of an organism. The opening of the archenteron to the exterior, which will later develop into the larval anus." []
xref: UBERON:0000100
is_a: ECAO:2000026 ! embryonic structure
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000494 ! archenteron

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000498
name: blastopore lip
def: "The margin (or edge) of the blastopore. In echinoderms, it is the circular rim of the blastopore and the transition zone between the invaginated archenteron and the outer epithelium of the embryo. Because cells move over the lip of the blastopore during echinoderm gastrulation, different populations of cells are located at the blastopore lip as gastrulation proceeds." []
synonym: "rim of blastopore" RELATED []
xref: UBERON:3010455
is_a: ECAO:2000001 ! anatomical structure
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000497 ! blastopore

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000499
name: mouth
def: "The most ventral portion of the digestive tract, containing the oral cavity." []
xref: UBERON:0000165
