id: ECAO:2000589
name: embryonic non-skeletogenic mesenchyme cell
def: "An embryonic cell that after undergoing an epithelial-to-mesenchymal transition in present in the blastocoel and will give rise to a non-skeletogenic mesenchyme derivative; e.g. pigment cells, blastocoelar cells, globular cells." []
synonym: "SMC" RELATED []
synonym: "secondary mesenchyme cell" RELATED []
is_a: ECAO:2000586 ! non-skeletogenic mesenchyme cell
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000588 ! embryonic non-skeletogenic mesenchyme

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000590
name: larval non-skeletogenic mesenchyme
def: "The non-skeletogenic mesenchyme that is present in a larva." []
is_a: ECAO:2000585 ! non-skeletogenic mesenchyme
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000012 ! larva

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000591
name: larval non-skeletogenic mesenchyme cell
def: "A larval cell that present in the blastocoel and participating in a non-skeletogenic mesenchyme derivative; e.g. pigment cells, blastocoelar cells, globular cells." []
is_a: ECAO:2000586 ! non-skeletogenic mesenchyme cell
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000590 ! larval non-skeletogenic mesenchyme

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000592
name: embryonic mesenchyme cell
def: "In echinoderms with no embryonic endoskeleton, all embryonic cells that have undergone an epithelial-to-mesenchymal transition and will participate in the elaboration of non-skeletogenic mesoderm derivatives; e.g. pigment cells, blastocoelar cells." []
is_a: ECAO:2000549 ! mesenchyme cell
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000547 ! mesoderm
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000008 ! embryo

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000593
name: larval mesenchyme cell
def: "In echinoderms with no larval endoskeleton, all larval mesenchyme cells that participate in the elaboration of non-skeletogenic mesoderm derivatives; e.g. pigment cells, blastocoelar cells." []
is_a: ECAO:2000549 ! mesenchyme cell
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000012 ! larva

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000594
name: oral presumptive non-skeletogenic mesoderm
def: "The presumptive embryonic non-skeletogenic mesoderm that in the vegetal plate is on the oral side of the embryo." []
synonym: "ventral presumptive embryonic non-skeletogenic mesoderm" RELATED []
synonym: "oral non-skeletogenic mesoderm" RELATED []
synonym: "ventral non-skeletogenic mesoderm" RELATED []
is_a: ECAO:2000582 ! presumptive non-skeletogenic mesoderm
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000053 ! vegetal hemisphere
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000492 ! vegetal plate

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000595
name: aboral presumptive non-skeletogenic mesoderm
def: "The presumptive embryonic non-skeletogenic mesoderm that in the vegetal plate is on the aboral side of the embryo." []
synonym: "dorsal presumptive embryonic non-skeletogenic mesoderm" RELATED []
synonym: "aboral non-skeletogenic mesoderm" RELATED []
synonym: "dorsal non-skeletogenic mesoderm" RELATED []
is_a: ECAO:2000582 ! presumptive non-skeletogenic mesoderm
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000053 ! vegetal hemisphere
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000492 ! vegetal plate

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000596
name: presumptive blastocoelar cell
def: "A cell that within the oral presumptive embryonic non-skeletogenic mesoderm will give rise to a blastocoelar cell." []
is_a: ECAO:2000582 ! presumptive non-skeletogenic mesoderm
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000492 ! vegetal plate
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000594 ! oral presumptive non-skeletogenic mesoderm

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000597
name: presumptive pigment cell
def: "A cell that within the aboral presumptive embryonic non-skeletogenic mesoderm will give rise to a pigment cell." []
synonym: "presumptive pigmented cell" RELATED []
synonym: "presumptive immunocyte" RELATED []
is_a: ECAO:2000582 ! presumptive non-skeletogenic mesoderm
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000492 ! vegetal plate
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000595 ! aboral presumptive non-skeletogenic mesoderm

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000598
name: immune cell
def: "A cell of the immune system that is involved in protecting the body against infectious disease and foreign invaders." []
synonym: "immunocyte" RELATED []
is_a: ECAO:2000549 ! mesenchyme cell
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000032 ! immune system

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000599
name: blastocoelar cell
def: "A class of migratory, non-skeletogenic mesenchyme cell, fibroblastic in appearance, which secrete extracellular matrix and exert immune cell functions." []
is_a: ECAO:2000598 ! immune cell
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000596 ! presumptive blastocoelar cell
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000006 ! multicellular organism

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000600
name: pigment cell
def: "A class of migratory, non-skeletogenic mesenchyme cell that produces visible pigment, usually reddish, and exert immune cell functions." []
xref: CL:0000147
is_a: ECAO:2000598 ! immune cell
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000597 ! presumptive pigment cell
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000006 ! multicellular organism

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000601
name: globular cell
def: "A subclass of blastocoelar cells; 10–15 μm in diameter, filled with large, flattened vesicles, and expressing a perforin-like marker (macpfA2)." []
is_a: ECAO:2000599 ! blastocoelar cell
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000599 ! blastocoelar cell
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000034 ! larval immune system

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000602
name: filopodial cell
def: "A heterogeneous subclass of blastocoelar cells; 5–7 μm in diameter, and with 2 to 5 filopodial projections that extend 10–50 μm. Filopodial cells are located in the blastocoel and across the basal surface of ectoderm and gut epithelia, and form multiple interconnected, syncytial networks." []
is_a: ECAO:2000599 ! blastocoelar cell
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000599 ! blastocoelar cell
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000034 ! larval immune system

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000603
name: phagocytic filopodial cell
def: "The subset of the filopodial cells that are phagocytic and express the immune effector gene 185/333." []
is_a: ECAO:2000602 ! filopodial cell
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000599 ! blastocoelar cell
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000034 ! larval immune system

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000604
name: ovoid cell
def: "A subclass of blastoceolar cells; 10–15 μm on their longest axis,  granular, oval-shaped, and non-syncytial. Ovoid cells arise in the blastocoel under some conditions of immune challenge, possibly from a morphological transformation of filopodial cells." []
is_a: ECAO:2000599 ! blastocoelar cell
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000599 ! blastocoelar cell
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000034 ! larval immune system

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000605
name: amoeboid cell
def: "A subclass of blastocoelar cells; 5-10 μm in size and comma-shaped. They are distinguishable by their rapid migration within the blastocoel and to sites of bacterial exposure." []
xref: CL:0000732
is_a: ECAO:2000599 ! blastocoelar cell
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000599 ! blastocoelar cell
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000034 ! larval immune system

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000606
name: presumptive muscle cell
def: "A cell present in the embryo that has the potential to give rise to a muscle cell." []
synonym: "muscle precursor cell" RELATED []
xref: CL:0000680
is_a: ECAO:2000584 ! non-skeletogenic mesoderm cell
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000492 ! vegetal plate
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000008 ! embryo

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000607
name: muscle
def: "The contractile tissue of an animal that is derived from mesoderm and contracts when stimulated thereby producing movement." []
synonym: "muscle organ" RELATED []
xref: UBERON:0001630
is_a: ECAO:2000021 ! tissue
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000547 ! mesoderm
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000043 ! muscular system

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000608
name: muscle cell
def: "A mature contractile cell that is part of a muscle and that is sometimes referred to as a muscle fiber or band due to its long and fibrous shape." []
synonym: "muscle band" RELATED []
synonym: "muscle fiber" RELATED []
synonym: "myocyte" RELATED []
xref: CL:0000187
is_a: ECAO:2000584 ! non-skeletogenic mesoderm cell
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000606 ! presumptive muscle cell
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000607 ! muscle

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000609
name: sphincter primordium
def: "An initial constriction within the archenteron marking where a sphincter will form." []
synonym: "sphincter constriction" RELATED []
synonym: "gut constriction" RELATED []
is_a: ECAO:2000532 ! constriction
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000008 ! embryo

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000610
name: sphincter
def: "A circular band of muscles that regulates the constriction or relaxation of a natural body passage or orifice for normal physiological functions." []
synonym: "sphincter muscle" RELATED []
synonym: "gastrointestinal sphincter" RELATED []
xref: UBERON:0004590
is_a: ECAO:2000607 ! muscle
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000029 ! digestive system

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000611
name: pyloric sphincter primordium
def: "The initial constriction within the archenteron that will develop into the pyloric sphincter and separates the midgut and hindgut." []
synonym: "pyloric sphincter constriction" RELATED []
synonym: "pyloric constriction" RELATED []
synonym: "midgut-hindgut constriction" RELATED []
is_a: ECAO:2000609 ! sphincter primordium
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000494 ! archenteron

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000612
name: pyloric sphincter
def: "The sphincter that in the larva separates the stomach from the intestine." []
synonym: "stomach-intestine constriction" RELATED []
xref: UBERON:0001202
is_a: ECAO:2000610 ! sphincter
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000611 ! pyloric sphincter primordium
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000031 ! larval digestive system

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000613
name: cardiac sphincter primordium
def: "The initial constriction within the archenteron that will develop into the cardiac sphincter and separates the foregut and the midgut." []
synonym: "cardiac sphincter constriction" RELATED []
synonym: "foregut-midgut constriction" RELATED []
synonym: "cardiac constriction" RELATED []
is_a: ECAO:2000609 ! sphincter primordium
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000494 ! archenteron

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000614
name: cardiac sphincter
def: "The sphincter that in the larva separates the stomach from the esophagus." []
synonym: "esophagus-stomach constriction" RELATED []
xref: FMA:14915
is_a: ECAO:2000610 ! sphincter
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000613 ! cardiac sphincter primordium
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000031 ! larval digestive system

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000615
name: anal sphincter primordium
def: "The initial constriction at the posterior end of the archenteron (i.e. at the level of the blastopore) that will develop into the anal sphincter." []
synonym: "anal sphincter contriction" RELATED []
synonym: "anal constriction" RELATED []
is_a: ECAO:2000609 ! sphincter primordium
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000494 ! archenteron
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000008 ! embryo

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000616
name: anal sphincter
def: "The sphincter that forms in the lava between the intestine  and the epidermis and encircle the anus." []
synonym: "intestin-ectoderm constriction" RELATED []
synonym: "anal pore" RELATED []
xref: UBERON:0004916
is_a: ECAO:2000610 ! sphincter
relationship: develops_from ECAO:2000615 ! anal sphincter primordium
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000031 ! larval digestive system

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000617
name: sphincter cell
def: "A cell that is part of a sphincter." []
synonym: "myoepithelial cell" RELATED []
is_a: ECAO:2000608 ! muscle cell
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000610 ! sphincter

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000618
name: pyloric sphincter cell
def: "A cell that is part of a pyloric sphincter." []
is_a: ECAO:2000617 ! sphincter cell
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000612 ! pyloric sphincter

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000619
name: cardiac sphincter cell
def: "A cell that is part of a cardiac sphincter." []
is_a: ECAO:2000617 ! sphincter cell
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000614 ! cardiac sphincter

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000620
name: anal sphincter cell
def: "A cell that is part of an anal sphincter." []
synonym: "anal pore muscle cell" RELATED []
is_a: ECAO:2000617 ! sphincter cell
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000616 ! anal sphincter

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000621
name: circumesophageal muscle
def: "Muscle strands that surround the larval esophagus." []
synonym: "esophagus muscle" RELATED []
is_a: ECAO:2000607 ! muscle
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000044 ! larval muscular system

[Term]
id: ECAO:2000622
name: circumesophageal muscle cell
def: "A cell that is part of the circumesophageal muscle." []
synonym: "presumptive circumesophageal muscle cell" RELATED []
is_a: ECAO:2000608 ! muscle cell
relationship: part_of ECAO:2000621 ! circumesophageal muscle

